{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/developing-today/code/pulls/7923","id":5217660299,"node_id":"PR_kwDOJWP4788AAAABNv8tiw","html_url":"https://github.com/developing-today/code/pull/7923","diff_url":"https://github.com/developing-today/code/pull/7923.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/developing-today/code/pull/7923.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/developing-today/code/issues/7923","commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/developing-today/code/pulls/7923/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/developing-today/code/pulls/7923/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/developing-today/code/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/developing-today/code/issues/7923/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/developing-today/code/statuses/8cb0d199a7648ead8cb65782b90ddd067dd6a2a6","number":7923,"state":"closed","locked":false,"title":"docs(id): decision record — semantic markup vocabulary v1 (#5849)","user":{"login":"dezren39","id":11225574,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjExMjI1NTc0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/11225574?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dezren39","html_url":"https://github.com/dezren39","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dezren39/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dezren39/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dezren39/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dezren39/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dezren39/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dezren39/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dezren39/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dezren39/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dezren39/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"## What this is\n\nThe decision record for **#5849** (semantic markup vocabulary v1), decomposition item 1 of the parent design **#5679** (markup & styling model for programs-as-websites). It settles the two things #5849 asks for — the v1 element set and the authoring syntax — and leaves the sibling-owned seams named rather than guessed.\n\n## Decisions\n\n- **Authoring syntax:** one HTML-shaped dialect from a **closed registry** of 32 elements. HTML names where HTML has the concept; quoted attributes only; text as content; no presentation attributes.\n- **Raw HTML boundary:** raw HTML/CSS is admitted only inside an explicit `<raw kind=\"html\">` / `<raw kind=\"css\">` region. A tag outside the registry is a build error with nearest-match suggestions, never an implicit raw pass-through.\n- **Element set:** document/structure (15), inline text (3), forms/actions (5), application chrome (9), with required attributes, a11y role, state set, child rules, and field/preference constraint sets.\n- **Target parity:** every element must render on web, custom-GUI and native targets; elements that could not get a defensible native meaning are deferred (trees, charts, rich text, canvas, maps, command palette, drag-and-drop, regex validation, i18n interpolation) with reasons.\n- **Accessibility by construction:** role, name source, state set, keyboard contract and focus order are registry properties; an unnamed interactive element cannot parse.\n- **Seams:** styling attaches through the single `assert` slot (#5850 owns the grammar, #5854 the cascade); bindings are fixed slots naming declared state/actions (#8) with no expressions or code; mapping is #5851, pipeline/conformance #5855.\n- **Safety:** every carried value enters only a text, quoted-attribute or sanitized-URL context per #5785 §1; no script context exists; emitted output is never parsed as source (keeps #2146's safe-rendering invariant).\n\nNo parent decision is changed; §11 lists the four questions that would require an explicit amendment on #5679 instead.\n\n## Evidence baseline\n\n`origin/main` at `30bd3a1398`, 2026-11-08. Issue #5849 OPEN with no linked PR or prior decision record; parent #5679 OPEN; siblings #5852/#5853/#5854 settled on main, #5850/#5851/#5855 OPEN. `git grep` over `pkgs/id` finds no existing registry or parser, so this is the first decision for this follow-on.\n\nDocs-only change: `doc/2026-11-08_decision_id5849_semantic_markup_vocabulary_v1.md`.\n\nCloses #5849.\n\n<!-- codesmith:footer -->\n---\n<a href=\"https://backend.blacksmith.sh/track/enable-autofix?expires=1796782686&installation_model_id=443529&pr_number=7923&ref=codesmith_pr_footer&repository=developing-today%2Fcode&return_to=https%3A%2F%2Fgithub.com%2Fdeveloping-today%2Fcode%2Fpull%2F7923&signature=d1537dcebd25a97e2a4c5063a4fcbddce98c4782ff3173264a55c965ff5dc45e\"><picture><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\" srcset=\"https://pr-comments-assets.blacksmith.sh/codesmith/autofix-with-codesmith-dark.svg\"><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: light)\" srcset=\"https://pr-comments-assets.blacksmith.sh/codesmith/autofix-with-codesmith-light.svg\"><img alt=\"Autofix with [code]smith\" src=\"https://pr-comments-assets.blacksmith.sh/codesmith/autofix-with-codesmith-dark-3x.png\" width=\"190\" height=\"28\"></picture></a>\n<sup><a href=\"https://app.blacksmith.sh/developing-today/codesmith/code/pr/7923?autoLogin=true&ref=codesmith_pr_footer\">Open in [code]smith</a> · Need help on this PR? Tag <code>@codesmith-bot</code> with what you need.</sup>\n\n<!-- codesmith:autofix:disabled -->\n<!-- /codesmith:footer -->","labels":[],"milestone":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"created_at":"2026-11-09T02:18:03Z","updated_at":"2026-11-09T03:34:43Z","closed_at":"2026-11-09T03:34:40Z","merged_at":"2026-11-09T03:34:40Z","merge_commit_sha":"2649012d0ea8fca2f0ed99d2c2408609a9dc1659","assignee":null,"assignees":[],"requested_reviewers":[],"requested_teams":[{"id":7767549,"node_id":"T_kwDOAZNvF84AdoX9","url":"https://api.github.com/organizations/2